WHO(1)                         P32W Unix                          WHO(1)

NAME
       who - who is logged in

SYNOPSIS
       who

DESCRIPTION
       who lists the users logged in, one line each: the name, the
       terminal and the time of login (local time, see tz(5)),
       read from /etc/utmp, which login(1) writes and init(8)
       clears when the session ends. Users who became someone else
       with su(1) are listed under their login name.

EXAMPLES
       $ who
       root     tty0     Oct 14 09:12
       ken      tty1     Oct 14 10:40

FILES
       /etc/utmp      the login records

EXIT STATUS
       0; 1 if /etc/utmp cannot be opened.

SEE ALSO
       id(1), whoami(1), login(1), uptime(1), utmp(5)

BUGS
       Arguments are ignored: there is no who am i, no -q or -H.
       Names and terminals longer than 8 characters are cut.
